.TH VAINFO 1 "2026-10-10" "libva-utils" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vainfo \- print information about the VA-API driver
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vainfo
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vainfo
prints information about the VA-API (Video Acceleration API) driver in use.
It reports the libva version, the vendor/driver version, and the video profiles
and entrypoints (decode, encode and video processing) that the driver supports.
It is the standard way to check whether hardware\-accelerated video decoding and
encoding are available on the system.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a usage message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
In addition to the profiles and entrypoints, print all supported attributes.
.TP
.BI \-\-display " display"
Query the given display instead of the default one. The special value
.B help
prints the list of available displays.
.TP
.BI \-\-device " device"
Use the given device node. This is only honoured by the
.B drm
display.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LIBVA_DRIVER_NAME
Select the VA-API driver to load (for example
.BR iHD " or " i965 ).
.TP
.B DISPLAY
The X11 or Wayland display to use, when the corresponding backend is enabled.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B vainfo
Show the driver version and the supported profiles and entrypoints.
.TP
.B vainfo \-\-all
Also show all supported attributes.
.SH SEE ALSO
The VA-API documentation:
.IR https://github.com/intel/libva .
